# <tag>[,<tag>...]: <Short title in imperative mood (max ~65 chars)>
#
# Examples of valid headers:
#   cpu: Refactor branch predictors
#   mem,mem-cache: Improve packet class readability
#   arch-arm,sim: Fix syscall emulation for ARM
#   misc: Add Dev Container configuration
#
# Rules enforced by ext/git-commit-msg:
#   * First line MUST start with one or more gem5 tags (see MAINTAINERS.yaml),
#     comma-separated, followed by ": " and a short title.
#   * No leading or trailing whitespace on the header.
#   * Second line MUST be blank.
#   * Body (optional but recommended) wraps at ~72 chars and explains the
#     WHAT and WHY of the change.
#   * Trailers like "Change-Id:", "Signed-off-by:", "Reviewed-by:" go last.
#
# --- Body (wrap at 72 chars) ---

# --- Trailers ---
# Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
